  "notes": [
    "Source: archive.org scan of Sega's 'Genesis Instruction Manual' (1993, US), page 4 'Identifying Parts' (the model 2 shell, confirmed in the page image); quotes are clean lines of the OCR text layer.",
    "media: 'Cartridge Slot' on the top face in the parts drawing: cartridge_top. controls: 'Power Button', 'Reset Button' (plus a 'Power-On Indicator', not a control).",
    "Envelope and mass: no maker or museum figure found.",
    "ports: page 4 'Identifying Parts' plus page 5 'BACK VIEW OF CONSOLE', filed as the complete list. Our mappings of the maker's wording: 'Control Port 1/2' -> controller_proprietary 2 (no connector standard named; coordinator ruling 2026-11-01); 'A/V OUT Jack' -> multi_av_out; 'AC Adaptor Jack' -> power_in; 'Extension Compartment' -> expansion. 'A/V OUT Jack' is transcribed from the page image; the others are clean OCR lines."
